[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Database Statistics (Gathering and Monitoring) in Oracle DB"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Database statistics are crucial for the Oracle optimizer to generate efficient execution plans. Gathering and monitoring these statistics ensures optimal database performance. This tutorial covers the process of gathering, monitoring, and managing database statistics in Oracle."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding Database Statistics"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Database statistics provide information about the data stored in the database. These statistics include table statistics (number of rows, blocks), column statistics (number of distinct values, data distribution), index statistics (number of leaf blocks, depth), and system statistics (CPU speed, I/O performance)."},{"order":5,"type":"subheading","text":"Gathering Database Statistics"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"Oracle provides the 'DBMS_STATS' package for gathering database statistics. This package offers various procedures to collect statistics at different levels (table, schema, database)."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Table Statistics: Gather statistics for a specific table."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Schema Statistics: Gather statistics for all objects in a schema."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Database Statistics: Gather statistics for the entire database."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"-- Gather table statistics
EXEC DBMS_STATS.GATHER_TABLE_STATS (
  ownname => 'YOUR_SCHEMA',
  tabname => 'YOUR_TABLE',
  estimate_percent => DBMS_STATS.AUTO_SAMPLE_SIZE,
  method_opt => 'FOR ALL COLUMNS SIZE AUTO'
);
"},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"-- Gather schema statistics
EXEC DBMS_STATS.GATHER_SCHEMA_STATS (
  ownname => 'YOUR_SCHEMA',
  estimate_percent => DBMS_STATS.AUTO_SAMPLE_SIZE,
  method_opt => 'FOR ALL COLUMNS SIZE AUTO'
);
"},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"-- Gather database statistics
EXEC DBMS_STATS.GATHER_DATABASE_STATS (
  estimate_percent => DBMS_STATS.AUTO_SAMPLE_SIZE,
  method_opt => 'FOR ALL COLUMNS SIZE AUTO'
);
"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Key parameters in 'DBMS_STATS' procedures:"},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'ownname': The schema name."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'tabname': The table name."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'estimate_percent': The percentage of rows to sample. 'DBMS_STATS.AUTO_SAMPLE_SIZE' lets Oracle determine the optimal sample size."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'method_opt': Specifies how column statistics are gathered. 'FOR ALL COLUMNS SIZE AUTO' is recommended for automatic determination of histograms."},{"order":18,"type":"subheading","text":"Monitoring Database Statistics"},{"order":19,"type":"paragraph","text":"Regularly monitoring database statistics is essential to identify stale or missing statistics. Stale statistics can lead to suboptimal execution plans and performance degradation."},{"order":20,"type":"paragraph","text":"Oracle provides data dictionary views to monitor statistics:"},{"order":21,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'DBA_TAB_STATISTICS': Table statistics."},{"order":22,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'DBA_TAB_COL_STATISTICS': Column statistics."},{"order":23,"type":"bullet_point","text":"'DBA_INDEX_STATISTICS': Index statistics."},{"order":24,"type":"code","text":"-- Check last analyzed date for a table
SELECT table_name, last_analyzed
FROM DBA_TAB_STATISTICS
WHERE owner = 'YOUR_SCHEMA'
AND table_name = 'YOUR_TABLE';
"},{"order":25,"type":"code","text":"-- Check column statistics
SELECT column_name, num_distinct, density
FROM DBA_TAB_COL_STATISTICS
WHERE owner = 'YOUR_SCHEMA'
AND table_name = 'YOUR_TABLE'
AND column_name = 'YOUR_COLUMN';
"},{"order":26,"type":"subheading","text":"Automating Statistics Gathering"},{"order":27,"type":"paragraph","text":"Oracle provides automated statistics gathering through the 'auto task' infrastructure. This feature automatically gathers statistics for objects with stale or missing statistics."},{"order":28,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can configure the auto task using the 'DBMS_AUTO_TASK_ADMIN' package."},{"order":29,"type":"code","text":"-- Enable auto statistics gathering
EXEC DBMS_AUTO_TASK_ADMIN.ENABLE (
  client_name => 'auto optimizer stats collection',
  operation => NULL
);
"},{"order":30,"type":"code","text":"-- Disable auto statistics gathering
EXEC DBMS_AUTO_TASK_ADMIN.DISABLE (
  client_name => 'auto optimizer stats collection',
  operation => NULL
);
"},{"order":31,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices"},{"order":32,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Gather statistics after significant data changes (e.g., large data loads, updates, deletes)."},{"order":33,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use 'DBMS_STATS.AUTO_SAMPLE_SIZE' for automatic sample size determination."},{"order":34,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use 'FOR ALL COLUMNS SIZE AUTO' for automatic histogram creation."},{"order":35,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Monitor statistics regularly and address stale or missing statistics promptly."},{"order":36,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Consider using automated statistics gathering for routine maintenance."},{"order":37,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":38,"type":"paragraph","text":"Properly gathering and monitoring database statistics is essential for maintaining optimal Oracle database performance. By using the 'DBMS_STATS' package and monitoring data dictionary views, you can ensure that the optimizer has accurate information to generate efficient execution plans."}]
